        text: 'A supplier of MES software (MES: the system that tracks orders and production on the floor) has these tests in its pipeline.\n\nUnit tests: 3,000 at an average of 0.02 seconds. That is 3,000 × 0.02 = 60 seconds, 1 minute.\nIntegration tests: 200 at 1.5 seconds. 200 × 1.5 = 300 seconds, 5 minutes.\nEnd-to-end tests: 20 at 45 seconds. 20 × 45 = 900 seconds, 15 minutes.\n\nTotal 21 minutes. The 20 end-to-end tests, less than 1% of all tests, take 15 of the 21 minutes. That is the reason for the pyramid: if you want a faster pipeline, look first at the slow tests at the top.',
