        text: 'A team of 6 developers is building a planning module for a machine builder. They work with feature branches of 3 weeks on average. Every 3 weeks there is a “merge week”: 2 developers spend 4 days resolving conflicts and hunting faults that only show up after the merge.\n\nStep 1, the cost: 2 developers × 4 days = 8 developer-days per 3 weeks. In 3 weeks the team has 6 × 15 = 90 working days. That is 8 / 90, about 9% of capacity, on merging alone.\n\nStep 2, the cause: the branches live so long that they drift far from the trunk.',
        ask: 'Which change do you propose, and which three things does the team need to make it safe?',
